  m_text: "As war broke out between the American colonies and Great Britain, they
    were forced to adjust and evolve their military.\n\nThis was previously defined
    by informal militia but as events around Boston became more tense, many communities
    in Massachusetts began to create more elite regiments. There regiments trained
    more frequently and as were expected to be ready quickly, \u201Cat a minute\u2019s
    warning...\u201D they became known as \u201CMinute Men.\u201D\n\nThese regiments
    were made of men from all economic and racial backgrounds and formed the backbone
    of the Revolutionary forces."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 1eb09b9f42fdb0347acde32a3de371b2, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 1188452189419906419, guid: 1eb09b9f42fdb0347acde32a3de371b2, type: 2}
